Flavio Cardone wrote:
> Hello -
> 
> how do you make a pudding farm? You hit one to make it multiply? But what if
> you kill it instead of getting it to divide?

So hit it with an orcish helmet or a key. The pudding will divide if hit 
by an IRON object.

> Second question:
> 
> horses can be eaten by everyone without penalty?

Yes.

> Can chaotics eat dogs and cats?

Only orcs and cavepeople can (not even a special case for East Asians 
and dogs).

> And their own pets? 

There is no penalty for eating non-domestic pets.

> Can chaotics sacrifice dogs and cats?

There is no penalty for sacrificing untamed dogs and cats. Pets (even 
former pets IIRC) OTOH may not be sacrificed, regardless of your alignment.

